buffet-menu (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Check boxes and radio buttons in the Buffet menu are drawn with the
    theme's background and border, as in the applications' own menus: in
    themes that draw the box that way, only the tick or the dot showed.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

buffet-menu (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release. Buffet Menu gives the GTK 3 applications you choose a
    header bar with a Buffet button, which shows all of their menus at
    once, laid out side by side, in place of the menu bar.
  * Each application has its own layout settings: one row, equal rows,
    two rows or a set number of menus per row, as wide as the window or
    the screen, and keyboard shortcuts next to the items, in tooltips or
    hidden.
  * A keyboard shortcut (Ctrl+Alt+N) opens the Buffet menu of the active
    window, and closes it again.
  * The menus open at once: they're loaded and laid out as soon as a
    window appears, and kept while they don't change.
  * Disabled items are greyed out, and ticks and choices follow the
    application.
  * Only the applications given the Buffet menu hide their menu bar, and
    only while Buffet Menu runs. It starts at login.
  * Draft translations into Spanish, French, German, and Brazilian
    Portuguese, waiting for a review by native speakers.

 -- Wesley Hayslip <xl_cheese@hotmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
